# E-type traffic: what a listen-only puck on "ibex" ch2 hears from OTHER pucks.
# Must parse as NotOurs and never mark the link alive. Source: synthetic,
# E1 layout from PROTOCOL.md §6 (with the [LEN][S1] header stripped).

# E1 host frame / discovery beacon: [E1][proteus 4][ibex 4][ch][0 0 0][base 4][prefix]
e1 01 02 03 04 05 06 07 08 02 00 00 00 11 22 33 44 55

# bare E3 input poll
e3 00

# REAL capture 2026-10-15: genuine Valve puck, controller OFF, discovery ch2,
# crc ok. 8 consecutive beacons ~4.03 ms apart were byte-identical (one bonded
# slot, no rotation); only S1 changed, cycling 0x02 0x04 0x06 0x00 (PID 1,2,3,0,
# no-ack bit clear). Layout matches PROTOCOL.md §6 exactly: 18 B, bytes 10..13
# zero. proteus 0x63513e7f, ibex 0x81f57117, session ch 6, base 65 1b ad f0
# (stored form), prefix 0x14.
e1 7f 3e 51 63 17 71 f5 81 06 00 00 00 65 1b ad f0 14
